<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine peso ends weak as Cent Bank buys dlrs.</title>
<headline>Philippine peso ends weak as Cent Bank buys dlrs.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>--------------------------- March 7-------------------------</p>
<p>* Central Bank seen buying $102 million</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The Philippine peso ended weak on Friday as the Central Bank dominated the market with its heavy dollar purchases, traders said.</p>
<p>The peso settled at 26.323 at the close of the day from 26.321, with the day's average at 26.320 from 26.321.</p>
<p>Volume swelled to $235.5 million from $157.6 million.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a continuation of the old story. There's still a lot of inflows. The Central Bank has to intervene,&quot; a dealer said.</p>
</text>
